cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DentalAI, please cite this repository and the DENTEX dataset."
title: "DentalAI: AI-Assisted Dental Radiography and Patient-History System"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "sayfeldinn"
    affiliation: "Alexandria University"
  - name: "Seif-shawky"
    affiliation: "Alexandria University"
# Two-person team. GitHub handles are used because they are the confirmed
# identifiers; display names can be substituted without changing the roster.
repository-code: "https://github.com/sayfeldinn/dental-xray-ai-assistant"
url: "https://github.com/sayfeldinn/dental-xray-ai-assistant"
abstract: >-
  DentalAI is an assistive clinical decision-support prototype for panoramic dental
  radiographs. A v3 pipeline combines a 32-class FDI tooth detector, a 4-class disease
  detector and geometric association; missing-teeth and 11-class findings models are
  advisory only. Every AI finding requires dentist confirmation before it enters a
  rule-based treatment and drug-safety workflow. The system is evaluated on the locked
  DENTEX validation split and an external Romanian hospital set; it is a research
  prototype, not a medical device.
keywords:
  - dental radiography
  - panoramic X-ray
  - object detection
  - clinical decision support
  - DENTEX
license: MIT
version: "3.0"
date-released: 2026-11-18
